  "notes": "{感|かん}じる means to feel, sense, or perceive through emotions or physical sensations.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nType: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive) - takes を for what is felt\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{感|かん}じている indicates an ongoing state of feeling: {疲|つか}れを{感|かん}じている (I'm feeling tired).\n\nPHYSICAL SENSATIONS:\n- {痛|いた}みを{感|かん}じる: to feel pain\n- {寒|さむ}さを{感|かん}じる: to feel cold\n- {暑|あつ}さを{感|かん}じる: to feel heat\n\nEMOTIONS:\n- {喜|よろこ}びを{感|かん}じる: to feel joy\n- {不安|ふあん}を{感|かん}じる: to feel anxiety\n- {責任|せきにん}を{感|かん}じる: to feel responsibility\n\nIMPRESSIONS (Sense 2):\nWhen expressing opinions: [na-adj]に{感|かん}じる or [clause]と{感|かん}じる\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}に{感|かん}じる: to find it strange\n- {必要|ひつよう}だと{感|かん}じる: to feel it's necessary\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {感|かん}じ: feeling, impression (noun)\n- {感覚|かんかく}: sense, sensation\n- {感動|かんどう}する: to be moved/touched",
